node_modules
.next
.git
# EVERY env file, not just the obvious ones. `.env` and `.env*.local` used to be
# the rule, which quietly let `.env.production` through — and Next loads that
# during `next build`, so the author's own Supabase URL ended up inlined in the
# browser bundle of an image meant to be handed to strangers. Caught by grepping
# a built image for it; nothing else would have said a word.
#
# The build needs none of these now: public config is read at runtime and
# injected per request (src/lib/public-config.ts), and secrets never were.
.env*
npm-debug.log*
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
README.md
.vercel
*.tsbuildinfo
